cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "mento: an intuitive tool for structural engineers to design concrete elements efficiently"
message: "If you use mento in your work, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Caballero
    given-names: "Mehdí"
    email: mihdicaballero@gmail.com
  - family-names: Romaris
    given-names: "Juan Pablo"
    email: jpromaris@yahoo.com.ar
repository-code: "https://github.com/mento-calc/mento"
url: "https://mento-docs.readthedocs.io/"
abstract: >-
  mento is a Python package for the design and verification of reinforced concrete elements
  — beams, one way slabs, shear walls and two way slab punching — according to ACI 318-19,
  EN 1992-2004 and CIRSOC 201-2025. It provides unit aware calculations, results as pandas
  DataFrames for batch work, and detailed calculation reports in Word.
keywords:
  - structural engineering
  - reinforced concrete
  - concrete design
  - structural analysis
  - ACI 318
  - Eurocode 2
  - CIRSOC 201
  - Python
license: MIT
version: 1.6.0
date-released: "2026-10-10"
identifiers:
  # Concept DOI: always resolves to the latest release, so it never has to change here.
  # The DOI of one specific release is on its own Zenodo record.
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21956634
    description: Concept DOI for all versions of mento
